    {
      "sentence_id": 1,
      "japanese": "最近は海外でも日本の食材が手に入りやすくなりました。",
      "english_translation": "Recently, it has become easier to obtain Japanese ingredients overseas."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 2,
      "japanese": "日本食のスーパーやアジア食品店に行かなくても、一般のスーパーでお醤油やお味噌、海苔やおせんべいも売っています。",
      "english_translation": "You don't need to go to Japanese supermarkets or Asian food stores; you can find soy sauce, miso, seaweed, and snacks in regular supermarkets as well."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 3,
      "japanese": "豆腐はふつうの食材として当たり前のように野菜のコーナーに並べられていますし、日本酒もワインの棚に並んでいます。",
      "english_translation": "Tofu is commonly available as a staple ingredient, just like vegetables, and sake is often found alongside wine."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 4,
      "japanese": "また、スーパーになくても、ネットで注文すればたいていの日本の食材は手に入ります。",
      "english_translation": "Furthermore, even if you can't find certain ingredients at a local supermarket, you can usually order them online and have them delivered to your home."
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 5,
      "japanese": "でも、日本の食材を手に入れるのが大変だった頃がありました。",
      "english_translation": "However, there was a time when it was difficult to obtain Japanese ingredients."
    }
